    <summary>Free, open-source file converter you use by dragging. 255 formats, offline, no Office needed.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Filee is a free, open-source file converter you use by dragging. Hold a key (Ctrl), drag files and drop them on a format in the donut that opens at your cursor.

## Features

- **Right at your cursor**: no app window to open. Only the formats that make sense for the files you drag appear.
- **255 formats, no other software**: images, PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, HWP/HWPX, e-books, archives, fonts, CAD, 3D models and geospatial data work without Office, Hancom Office or LibreOffice.
- **Stays on your computer**: nothing is uploaded. Filee works offline and saves the result next to the original.
- **Many files at once**, in parallel, with presets for quality, size, DPI, PDF pages, compression, video and audio.
- **Watch folders**, the Explorer right-click menu, a keyboard shortcut, a drop zone and the `filee` command line.

Optional engines (FFmpeg, LibreOffice, Ghostscript, Pandoc, calibre) are downloaded by Filee only when needed.

## Package parameters

By default the installer adds the File Explorer menu, starts Filee at sign-in and puts the `filee` command on PATH, as the interactive installer does.

- `/NoContextMenu` - don't add Filee to the File Explorer right-click menu
- `/NoStartup` - don't start Filee when you sign in
- `/NoCli` - don't add the `filee` command to PATH
- `/DesktopIcon` - add a desktop shortcut

Example: `choco install filee --params "'/NoStartup /DesktopIcon'"`

The menu and startup options only apply to a first install. Updates keep what you chose in Filee (Settings → General).

## Notes

- Windows 10 (1809) or later, 64-bit only.
- Setup starts Filee in the notification area when it finishes.
- Filee can also update itself. Upgrading with Chocolatey works either way.
- Uninstalling keeps your settings in `%APPDATA%\Filee`.
]]></description>
